src/**
tsconfig.json
.vscode/**
*.map
.gitignore

# node_modules is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# The extension resolves the engine at runtime with `await import('vecline')`,
# so the engine has to travel inside the .vsix — there is no install step on the
# user's machine to fetch it. Ignoring node_modules produced a 13 KB package of
# eight files with no engine in it at all, which installs fine and then fails on
# first use with "Cannot find module 'vecline'".
#
# vsce walks the production dependency tree from package.json and includes only
# that, so devDependencies (typescript, @types/*) stay out without needing a
# rule here. The package is large because the engine carries native decoders
# with per-platform prebuilds; that is the cost of the extension working
# offline, which is the whole point of it.
